{"title":"Career Roadmap · Linear Accelerator Operator","role":"Linear Accelerator Operator","summary":"A Linear Accelerator (LINAC) Operator works in a radiation oncology department and supports the safe, accurate delivery of external-beam radiation therapy using a medical linear accelerator.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Linear Accelerator (LINAC) Operator works in a radiation oncology department and supports the safe, accurate delivery of external-beam radiation therapy using a medical linear accelerator."},{"type":"h","text":"The role involves:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Preparing patients for radiation treatment"},{"text":"Verifying treatment information and patient identity"},{"text":"Operating LINAC systems under approved clinical protocols"},{"text":"Positioning and immobilizing patients"},{"text":"Performing treatment-room safety checks"},{"text":"Following radiation-safety procedures"},{"text":"Monitoring patients during treatment"},{"text":"Recording treatment delivery"},{"text":"Working with radiation oncologists, medical physicists and radiotherapy technologists"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important qualification note","text":"A generic B.Sc/BPT/BOT/BMLT degree does not automatically qualify someone to operate a medical LINAC. For this career, the candidate should have a recognized/appropriate Radiotherapy Technology or Radiation Therapy qualification and meet applicable institutional, professional and regulatory requirements."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Direction"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Radiotherapy Technology fundamentals, clinical internship, LINAC operation training"}],[{"text":"2030–2034"},{"text":"Radiotherapy Technologist / LINAC Operator"}],[{"text":"2034–2040"},{"text":"Senior Radiotherapy Technologist / LINAC 